    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Here, \uD835\uDC6202 is an initial guess and \uD835\uDC62\uD835\uDC56\uD835\uDC5B(\uD835\uDC61) approximates \uD835\uDC62\uD835\uDC56(\uD835\uDC61) = \uD835\uDC62(\uD835\uDC61)|Ω\uD835\uDC56(\uD835\uDC61). Note that the Robin– Robin method is sequential, but the computation of each \uD835\uDC62\uD835\uDC56\uD835\uDC5B can be implemented in parallel when Ω\uD835\uDC56(\uD835\uDC61) is a union of nonadjacent subdomains, as is the case in Figure 1."
  }, {
